The accounts list
01-accounts-and-security
Every registered account except SDSYS, one to a row. Starts in is where a session in that account begins: menu is the home screen, terminal is the command prompt, and default (menu) or default (terminal) means the account has no setting of its own and follows the system default.
Own says whether the account may add programs of its own to its home screen. Tiles off lists the tiles you have turned off for it; a plus sign at the end means the list is longer than the column.
Select an account with the Up and Down keys or a click, then press Tab to change its settings. F1 or ? on any row of the Menu box explains that setting.
